WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.649 --> 00:00:05.430
Welcome back to Curious Archive.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:11.300
This video is a new chapter in my long-running
series exploring the incredible speculative

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:15.620
evolution saga of Serina, the world of birds.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.450
Serina was created by the talented artist
and worldbuilder Dylan Bajda — and many

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:26.140
extraordinary developments have occurred since
we last explored this distant moon.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:32.150
The triumphs and tragedies, the joys and the
sorrows of this era are perhaps greater than

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:33.840
any that have come before.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:39.780
So, for this entry into the archive, we’ll
chronicle the rise and fall of fascinating

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:46.320
species, and discover astonishing revelations
as the world of Serina creeps ever closer

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.920
to its end…

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:55.670
…Two-hundred and seventy million years since
the story began, we have now entered the Late

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:02.280
Ocean Age, an era where the encroachment of
ice is at its worst yet — with a shallow,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:07.920
vegetated equatorial ocean now the last haven
for most species on Serina.

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:14.430
When we left off, the Gravediggers and Daydreamers
had joined forces and established a unified

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:15.510
society.

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:21.140
With the battle against the Warmongers becoming
a faint memory, these two species will create

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:26.560
a culture that will persist on a timescale
greater than any that came before.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:33.190
Over the coming era, Gravediggers and Daydreamers
will transform the equatorial ocean into a

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:34.190
paradise.

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:39.920
With deep knowledge of the principles of ecology,
they become ecosystem engineers, carefully

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:45.220
influencing the evolution of other species
to ensure the environment remains stable.

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:51.360
And a third intelligent species has joined
their alliance, one descended from the earlier

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:57.310
Luddies, a playful herbivore species who have
been growing more and more intelligent.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:03.880
And after millions of years of co-evolution,
the Luddies have now become the wise Greenskeepers.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:10.299
Together, these three remarkable species — collectively
called the Sea Stewards, will influence the

00:02:10.299 --> 00:02:15.560
path of all creatures that swim in this shallow
ocean.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:21.150
One of the most extreme examples of a species
whose evolution has been shaped by the Sea

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.930
Stewards’ influence is the Floating Bloat.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:30.689
Over 140 feet, or 42 meters in length, this
herbivore is the largest creature to evolve

00:02:30.689 --> 00:02:35.120
on Serina, eclipsing the length and weight
of blue whales on Earth.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.599
The Bloat is now so large that it is too buoyant
to fully submerge itself, instead floating

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:45.919
along like a boat with its elongated neck
dipping below the sea to feed on thousands

00:02:45.919 --> 00:02:48.409
of pounds of vegetation per-day.

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:54.170
A semi-domesticated animal, the Floating Bloat
serves as a source of food and raw material

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:59.939
for the Sea Stewards, yet lives a life of
relative bliss.

00:02:59.939 --> 00:03:04.319
Another species much changed by the Sea Stewards
presence are the Aukvultures.

00:03:04.319 --> 00:03:10.099
A type of seraph, the Aukvultures are one
of the last descendants of the Archangles

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:12.720
that once ruled Serina’s skies.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:18.459
Like Earth vultures, Aukvultures have converged
upon a scavenger niche, feeding off the scrap

00:03:18.459 --> 00:03:20.859
piles of the Sea Stewards.

00:03:20.859 --> 00:03:26.750
This behavior has caused the Aukvultures to
become unusually intelligent, able to manipulate

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:31.010
Gravediggers into offering them scraps by
performing simple tricks.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:35.120
They’re a lineage to keep an eye on.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:39.680
Within this engineered ecosystem, many species
remain wild.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.340
One of the more fascinating keystone lineages
of this era are the Sealumps.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:50.169
An offshoot of the Land Trunkos we’ve seen
in past eras, Sealumps managed to escape the

00:03:50.169 --> 00:03:54.709
ice-scarred mainland to the lush underwater
Eden just beyond the shore.

00:03:54.709 --> 00:04:01.939
Now a specialized marine subspecies, the Sealumps
have become a keystone lineage in the shallow

00:04:01.939 --> 00:04:03.629
oceans.

00:04:03.629 --> 00:04:07.069
One species seems more changed than any other.

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:13.430
The Sea Shoggoths, once mighty predators feared
by all, now function as a garbage disposal

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:14.430
service.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:19.530
Fed by the Sea Stewards’ regular supply
of waste, these terrifying ant colonies have

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:23.650
learned not to attack the providers of their
consistent meals.

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:26.880
But the Sea Shoggoths have not been tamed
by this partnership.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.630
They have only been made smarter.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:34.720
The colonies know that for now, the path of
least resistance is waiting passively for

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:36.699
offerings of garbage.

00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:41.990
But if this uneasy contract is ever terminated,
the Sea Shoggoths will not hesitate to do

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:45.770
whatever they need to survive…

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:52.110
Over the next several million years, Sea Steward
society remains remarkably unchanged, as the

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:58.400
foundations of their civilization are ecologically
sustainable and not inclined to technological

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.400
shifts.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:03.990
And the ancient Daydreamer prophecy, which
told of three different essences of a deity

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:09.449
creator — land, water, and air — finding
each other once again, has now been largely

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:11.460
relegated to a myth.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:16.400
In all their travels, Sea Stewards have never
encountered flying lifeforms with advanced

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:23.390
intelligence, so many assume the third essence
never existed after all...

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:27.009
Yet there are regions the Sea Stewards have
yet to chart.

00:05:27.009 --> 00:05:31.759
Few species from the shallow sea venture past
the southernmost islands.

00:05:31.759 --> 00:05:36.739
But this young Glacial Foxtrotter — the
last of the three-legged canithere lineage

00:05:36.739 --> 00:05:40.500
— is about to stumble upon a forgotten land.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:45.970
Crossing a newly-formed bridge of sea ice,
the Foxtrotter reaches the southern continent

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:47.889
of Serinaustra.

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:52.000
This frozen region is a wasteland, yet it
is not uninhibited.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:58.539
A few creatures eke out their lives in Serina’s
least welcoming environment — like the fearsome

00:05:58.539 --> 00:05:59.729
Snowscrounger.

00:05:59.729 --> 00:06:05.400
These scavengers are the single living descendent
of the Squork, a tentacle-bird lineage that

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:10.010
hasn’t been as successful as the Trunkos
in adapting to the changing world.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:15.240
The Snowscrounger’s presence makes life
on Serinaustra an uneasy prospect for the

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.099
lone Foxtrotter.

00:06:17.099 --> 00:06:22.090
Against all odds though, it will establish
a place here—and will not be the last Foxtrotter

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.360
to do so...

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:28.409
Yet Serinaustra isn’t the only frozen wasteland
on Serina.

00:06:28.409 --> 00:06:34.289
Its northern counterpart, the continent of
Serinarcta, is home to a long-lost relative

00:06:34.289 --> 00:06:36.720
of the ocean-going Gravedigger.

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:42.410
The Savage Gravediggers are hulking predators
that lost the spark of sapience in favor of

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.180
physical strength.

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:49.960
Rumors of these monsters form the basis of
campfire stories among the ocean-going Gravediggers,

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:54.139
although few believe the stories to be true...

00:06:54.139 --> 00:06:59.160
And there is another remarkable species on
Serinarcta that has slipped the detection

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.949
of the Sea Stewards.

00:07:00.949 --> 00:07:06.930
The Blue-Tailed Chatteravens are a territorial
and often aggressive omnivore species that

00:07:06.930 --> 00:07:09.939
are nonetheless abnormally intelligent.

00:07:09.939 --> 00:07:14.669
For the Chatteravens are the descendants of
the White-Margined Chatterers — a species

00:07:14.669 --> 00:07:17.659
notable for being the pet of the Last Woodcrafter.

00:07:17.659 --> 00:07:23.729
And the Chatterers are, in turn, distantly
evolved from the Babbling Jays — the first

00:07:23.729 --> 00:07:29.979
advanced intelligent life to emerge on Serina
for a brief time all those eons ago.

00:07:29.979 --> 00:07:35.449
In the present, Chatteravens are intelligent
enough to possess a rudimentary language,

00:07:35.449 --> 00:07:38.270
but none of them are truly sapient.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.509
That is, except for one.

00:07:40.509 --> 00:07:45.719
Brighteye is a young chatterraven with a rare
mutation that allows for abstract thinking

00:07:45.719 --> 00:07:47.039
and imagination.

00:07:47.039 --> 00:07:51.900
He is a genetic throwback, having regained
the spark of his ancestral species.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:55.219
And he isn’t the only mutant in his family.

00:07:55.219 --> 00:08:01.749
His brother, whose name translates to Whitecrown,
was born an outcast due to his lack of pigment.

00:08:01.749 --> 00:08:07.340
Unwelcome within the brutal Chatterraven hierarchy,
the two siblings set off on their own across

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:08.340
Serinarcta.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.319
While isolated in this harsh wilderness, they
at least have each other.

00:08:12.319 --> 00:08:16.469
And Brighteye has seen things he can’t explain
to his younger brother.

00:08:16.469 --> 00:08:21.819
Visions of species he doesn’t recognize,
and whispers from a mysterious voice telling

00:08:21.819 --> 00:08:23.060
him he’s not alone.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:28.669
And though neither knows it yet, the actions
of Brighteye and Whitecrown will change Serina

00:08:28.669 --> 00:08:32.479
for millions of years to come.

00:08:32.479 --> 00:08:37.070
Many dangers await the brothers in the snowy
wilds of Seinarcta.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:43.370
On silent, fur-lined wings, the startling
Snowspirit stalks prey like a vengeful ghost.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:49.310
The ice-age descendant of the early-ultimocene
tribbats, Snowspirits fortunately rarely go

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:52.010
for prey larger than rats.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:57.580
Like barn owls, they are nocturnal hunters,
and have convergently evolved a facial disc

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:58.940
to improve their hearing.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:06.390
In the winter darkness, spotting a Snowspirit’s
large, expressive eyes is a frightening sight.

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:09.530
Yet there are larger predators than Snowspirits.

00:09:09.530 --> 00:09:14.620
Scissorjaws — the last species of the once
thriving circuagodogs (sir-quaggo-dogs) — are

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.690
hunters with asymmetrical jaws capable of
bringing down large predators.

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:23.680
The Scissorjaws, though, are on the absolute
brink of extinction.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:29.090
For they are being systematically hunted by
a force they cannot hope to understand.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:35.350
While journeying across the ice, the brothers
encounter the body of a fallen Scissorjaw.

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:40.350
While Whitecrown takes the free meal without
question, Brightyeye can’t help but wonder:

00:09:40.350 --> 00:09:43.710
what kind of predator hunts without eating
their prey?

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.370
Soon, the brothers find the answer.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:50.620
A wooly giant roams not far from the fallen
Scissorjaw.

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:55.710
Brighteye recognizes it as a plant eater,
and, more-remarkably, notices what appears

00:09:55.710 --> 00:09:58.120
to be a tool in its trunk-like beak.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:04.600
And when their eyes meet, Brighteye recognizes
something else — the spark of intelligence.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:10.170
This is a Wolly Wumpo, the largest living
land animal of this age, and one of the most

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.170
intelligent.

00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:15.790
At long last, sapience has struck within the
tentacle bird lineage.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:21.180
The Wooly Whumpos possess a unique language
and can use tools, but they are fearful of

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:26.650
outside dangers, eliminating the Scissorjaws
due to the potential threat they posed.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:29.940
And Wumpos have good reason to be wary.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:35.510
Not only are their numbers few, but they are
sometimes hunted by none other than the Chatteravens.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:40.620
On their own, a flock of Chatteravens has
no hope of taking down a Wumpo, but they have

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:42.490
a grim hunting strategy.

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:48.260
By singing in eerie harmony, they can alert
large predators to the location of lone Wumpos

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:52.240
— and then feed on any scraps left behind.

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:55.170
But Brighteye isn’t like most Chatteravens.

00:10:55.170 --> 00:11:00.350
Through silent gestures, he is able to convince
the Wumpo — an elder whose name roughly

00:11:00.350 --> 00:11:03.820
translates to ‘Blaze’ — that he means
her no harm.

00:11:03.820 --> 00:11:07.920
And what’s more, Brighteye is able to indicate
his intelligence.

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:11.850
From here on out, their lives are intertwined.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:16.530
Convincing the other Wumpos that the two Chatteravens
aren’t a threat isn’t an easy task for

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:20.250
Blaze, as their society has long been fearful
of outsiders.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:26.350
But Blaze knows that, somehow, these Chatteravens
are special.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:30.720
Communication between such separate lineages
isn’t easy, as Brighteye can’t register

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.740
most of the sounds that make up the Wumpo
language.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:39.180
But like the Gravediggers and Woodcrafters
long before them, they find a way.

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:44.120
Through the use of symbolic drawings, Brighteye
and Blaze break down the communication barrier

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:47.330
— inventing a unique language of pictograms.

00:11:47.330 --> 00:11:52.720
Soon, other Whumpos learn to do the same,
and a new world of possibilities opens up

00:11:52.720 --> 00:11:55.390
between them…

00:11:55.390 --> 00:12:01.000
At the same time, the Sea Stewards have come
to a grim realization that all other species

00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:07.050
on Serina are blissfully unaware of: The planet
is freezing over, and soon the ocean will

00:12:07.050 --> 00:12:08.760
be uninhabitable.

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:13.460
But if there’s anything the Sea Stewards
excel at, it’s cooperation towards a common

00:12:13.460 --> 00:12:14.460
goal.

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:18.340
And there are rumors that the Gravediggers
of the northern coasts have discovered something

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:21.000
beneath the ground that might help.

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:26.190
Traveling to the north, the Stewards discover
vast deposits of peat and coal.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:32.000
Formed from remains of ancient tropical swamps,
these deposits also house the bones of huge

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:37.410
and terrifying animals that roamed across
Serina millions of years ago.

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:42.280
Transporting these materials to the southern
ice sheets requires an engineering project

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:47.890
of an unmatched scale, but the Stewards are
determined to save the sea.

00:12:47.890 --> 00:12:52.430
Transporting thousands of tons of material
to the expanding glaciers and setting them

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:56.740
ablaze, the Stewards begin to experience some
success.

00:12:56.740 --> 00:13:01.670
But the region their mines are located in
is a perilous one, home to the monsters of

00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:05.360
their myths — demons that look like they
do, but attack without mercy.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:10.580
Their project cannot be completed quickly
enough…

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:14.180
Yet unbeknownst to the miners, they are being
watched.

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:19.270
Brighteye is curious about these new arrivals,
but Blaze sees them as monsters.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:24.910
For there is a legend that all Wumpos know,
that tells of an evil that came from the sea.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:31.260
Generations prior, the Gravediggers made landfall
and began to hunt the Wumpos — not recognizing

00:13:31.260 --> 00:13:32.480
their intelligence.

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:38.060
In retaliation, one Wumpo stole fire from
the Gravediggers to drive them back — but

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:43.870
couldn’t control the wild substance, and
caused the destruction of the herd and themselves.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:49.820
Now, all Wumpos fear the Gravediggers — and
the fire they command.

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:51.620
But Brighteye isn’t convinced.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:56.920
He believes the fire could be an asset to
the Wumpos and himself, if only they could

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:58.290
learn to make it.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:03.110
And as a descendent of a speech-mimicking
bird, through careful practice, he is able

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:06.610
to ask the Gravediggers directly how they
make fire.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:11.990
One can only imagine how the first Gravediggers
reacted to hearing a talking bird — a scene

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.950
right out of their oldest prophecy.

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:19.970
And unbeknownst to Brighteye, his actions
will ignite more than just coal…

00:14:19.970 --> 00:14:24.380
Word of a talking bird spreads like wildfire
among the Sea Stewards.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:30.850
At last, the prophecy seems to be upon them—the
third essence of their deity—the wings—having

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.020
seemingly arrived.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:36.950
So, when Brighteye asks the Sea Stewards to
give fire to the Wumpos and leave them in

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.510
peace, who are they to say no?

00:14:39.510 --> 00:14:44.570
The Steward’s engineering project is nearly
complete, and with the danger of ice on the

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:48.160
decline, sharing fire seems like little consequence.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:52.070
And far away, a presence watches all this
unfold.

00:14:52.070 --> 00:14:57.190
Some of what it sees impresses the observer,
yet other things have it worried.

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:01.700
With the mass-extraction of coal, a Pandora's
box was now open.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:08.010
For the first time in 270 million years of
its observation, something has arisen within

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:11.580
the project that has the potential to destroy
it.

00:15:11.580 --> 00:15:12.860
Time passes.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:18.190
The Wumpos use the gift of fire to drive back
any predators that threaten the herd.

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:22.930
Whitecrown eventually departs, guided by instinct
to return to the wild.

00:15:22.930 --> 00:15:28.450
In time, Blaze departs too, the elder Wumpo
passing away peacefully.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:34.180
Brighteye mourns his loss, and becomes increasingly
frustrated with the strange expectations of

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:35.930
the Sea Stewards.

00:15:35.930 --> 00:15:42.160
Then, to his horror, Brighteye discovers a
growing wildfire sweeping across the land.

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:47.090
The Chatteravens, following the example of
his brother Whitecrown, have learned to use

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:49.620
fire to hunt — but they can’t control
it.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:56.040
The fire spreads to an underground coal seam,
and an apocalyptic chain reaction begins.

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:01.240
Like the ancient Wumpo who thought they could
control fire, Brighteye now realizes the depths

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:02.540
of his mistake.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:07.550
In perhaps the greatest tragedy in all of
Serina’s history, the inferno spreads for

00:16:07.550 --> 00:16:10.900
miles across the land, all the way to the
sunset.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:17.260
And so, this chapter of the world ends not
with ice, but with fire.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:22.680
From miles away, the Sea Stewards can see
the fire too, and know their world is coming

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:23.880
to an end.

00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:29.890
And from far away, the observer, the one who
has overseen this experiment since the beginning,

00:16:29.890 --> 00:16:32.650
feels something it isn’t supposed to feel.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.100
It feels guilty.

00:16:34.100 --> 00:16:39.550
By whispering to Brighteye that he was not
alone all those years ago, it interfered,

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:42.360
and now everything had fallen apart.

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:47.660
Dying on a smoldering beach, Brighteye hears
the observer’s voice again.

00:16:47.660 --> 00:16:51.840
It apologizes for all the suffering its curiosity
caused.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:58.780
But Brighteye doesn’t care, and with his
last breath, he spits a curse at his creator…

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:05.000
On the southern iceshelf, a lone Snowscrounger
notices the sky glows a brilliant orange.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:09.620
It has no way of knowing a global apocalypse
is consuming Serina.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:15.180
But the observer knows what is to come, just
as it knows everything that came before.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:20.240
Over the course of Serina’s history, the
observer has witnessed many tragedies.

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:24.700
Seen many brilliant sparks go out, and never
has it interfered.

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:29.950
Yet this tragedy was the indirect result of
its own meddling, and as the observer reflects

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:35.890
on the last living moments of one brave little
bird, it makes a decision it has never before

00:17:35.890 --> 00:17:36.890
made.

00:17:36.890 --> 00:17:39.390
To offer help.

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:44.600
Appearing to the surviving Sea Stewards as
an amalgamation of many sapient species, the

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:46.270
observer speaks.

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:50.770
It tells them their world is ending because
of the consequences of the choices it made.

00:17:50.770 --> 00:17:53.530
So now, it is giving them a choice.

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:58.990
The Sea Stewards can go to a planet just like
the one they know, except where the fire never

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:01.550
happened, and the ice will not close in.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:08.010
So that one far and distant day their descendants
will swim across a far wider sea (stars).

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:11.450
The Sea Stewards accept.

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:16.470
The Sea Stewards awaken to a calm night, having
forgotten all they have seen.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:20.430
To them, nothing has changed, and not a moment
has passed.

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:25.720
The observer has solved its conundrum — splitting
off the sea stewards and cloning their familiar

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:30.930
world to colonize a new project as a compromise
for its interference.

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:36.860
On this new world, the Sea Stewards’ culture
is now free to advance…

00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:41.420
Yet far away, back on Serina, the experiment
isn’t over yet.

00:18:41.420 --> 00:18:46.370
With the observer returning to its impartial
surveillance, Serina is left to see through

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:49.150
another mass extinction on its own.

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:54.360
With its major keystone species effectively
gone in an instant, the consequences will

00:18:54.360 --> 00:19:01.540
be severe as Serina at last closes the door
on one chapter, and enters its final age…

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:07.300
Six hours into the Late-Ultimocene, the dawn
rises on a world without the Sea Stewards.

00:19:07.300 --> 00:19:12.860
Ravenous Nimicorn Thorngrazers feed on the
bodies of animals claimed by the fire, which

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:15.780
continues to burn through the coal seams beneath
the earth.

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:21.940
In time, the Sea Shoggoths — no longer provided
with regular meals, will revert to their ancestral

00:19:21.940 --> 00:19:22.940
condition.

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:28.770
And so, Serina enters a wild era where for
now only the toughest living things will be

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.060
rewarded.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:35.740
The mighty bloats are one of the first species
to vanish from this new world.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:41.690
With no natural defenses against horrors like
the Sea Shoggoths, they make for easy targets.

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:47.100
In just a few centuries, only the skeletons
of these mighty oceanic titans remain.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:52.730
As Serina warms and the ice melts, the oceans
grow deeper, and decaying plant life adapted

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:59.980
for the shallows turns the seas toxic — resulting
in almost 95% of ocean life becoming extinct.

00:19:59.980 --> 00:20:03.940
On land, a great thaw has begun.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:09.040
Duck-billed sealumps — the only sealump
species still capable of walking — arrive

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:14.520
in large numbers on Serinaustra, fleeing the
collapsing oceanic ecosystem.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:20.090
The Foxtrotters that arrived here just five
centuries ago find food is more plentiful,

00:20:20.090 --> 00:20:22.710
as do the Snowscroungers.

00:20:22.710 --> 00:20:28.940
In Serinarcta, the ice has also retreated,
allowing for a rise in biodiversity.

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:33.050
Yet the loss of the glaciers brings forth
its own dangers.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:38.730
Millions of years of built-up ice exerted
an extreme force upon Serina's crust, creating

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:41.490
concentrated subsurface pockets.

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:47.050
With the pressure now relieved, the plains
have been transformed into a deadly minefield.

00:20:47.050 --> 00:20:52.059
Over the coming eons, volcanoes will come
to life after tens of millions of years of

00:20:52.059 --> 00:20:56.970
dormancy, which will result in even more rapid
warming.

00:20:56.970 --> 00:21:00.470
Yet Serina, eventually, begins to heal.

00:21:00.470 --> 00:21:05.710
Several millennia later, there are few visible
signs of the Sea Stewards civilization left,

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:10.680
with the occasional exception of a Gravedigger
knife or a shard of pottery exposed through

00:21:10.680 --> 00:21:11.680
erosion.

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:15.150
Their legacy though, has left one final mark
on Serina.

00:21:15.150 --> 00:21:20.160
The Aukvulture — always an intelligent species
that learned to perform tricks in exchange

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:26.040
for food — has evolved to be even smarter
now that they must fend for themselves.

00:21:26.040 --> 00:21:29.250
Most Aukvultures are highly intelligent for
an animal.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:34.500
But among a small population — which refer
to themselves as reapers — a fluke of nature

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:38.520
has caused the spark of Sapience to arise
once more.

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:43.900
The reapers are a spiritual, melancholy group
who know their kind is not likely long for

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.070
this world.

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:51.370
Yet one reaper, whom we will call Eve, will
play a central role in a story unlike any

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:53.480
other...

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:57.230
The story begins in the atmosphere above Serina.

00:21:57.230 --> 00:22:01.140
Something that looks like a comet from the
surface is circling the moon.

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:06.240
Two pods detach and crash-land on the ground,
sustaining heavy damage.

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:11.110
These mysterious probes are perhaps the first
new stimulus to enter the closed system of

00:22:11.110 --> 00:22:14.980
Serina in over 270 million years.

00:22:14.980 --> 00:22:20.559
Losing connection to the host satellite, they
are now very much alone.

00:22:20.559 --> 00:22:25.380
One of these bizarre probes sets out from
the crash site, searching for the other.

00:22:25.380 --> 00:22:30.710
From the sky, the reaper known as Eve watches
the strange star-creature with curiosity.

00:22:30.710 --> 00:22:36.320
She’s never seen anything like this being
that moves like a living thing, yet doesn’t

00:22:36.320 --> 00:22:37.770
seem to be alive.

00:22:37.770 --> 00:22:43.360
Soon, the autonomous probe finds their sibling
has not survived the crash.

00:22:43.360 --> 00:22:47.850
They will have to explore this strange world
all on their own.

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:53.260
But Eve follows the being, which she names
Fellstar, on their journey across the uncharted

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:54.260
surface.

00:22:54.260 --> 00:23:00.320
For she is alone as well — having not seen
another intelligent Reaper in over a decade.

00:23:00.320 --> 00:23:05.611
At first, Fellstar spends their time cataloguing
the world around them with mechanical indifference.

00:23:05.611 --> 00:23:12.490
But in time, they take notice of Eve, who
points out native species to the curious robot.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:16.920
Over time, Fellstar’s personality grows
bigger, and they learn to communicate with

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:19.980
Eve through gestures and imitation.

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:24.140
Across the widest chasms, they forge an unbreakable
bond.

00:23:24.140 --> 00:23:29.500
Two lonely souls, isolated by space and by
time, ultimately find whatever they need in

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:30.500
each other.

00:23:30.500 --> 00:23:34.750
They travel for many seasons, and find there
is much to live for.

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:41.070
Eventually, Fellstar no longer seems to remember
how - or why - they came here.

00:23:41.070 --> 00:23:46.350
The story never directly states what kind
of intelligent life made Fellstar, but given

00:23:46.350 --> 00:23:52.050
their avian appearance and gentle nature,
it seems likely Fellstar is an emissary from

00:23:52.050 --> 00:23:53.929
the Sea Stewards planet.

00:23:53.929 --> 00:23:59.180
While the Sea Stewards no longer remember
Serina, and having lost contact with Fellstar

00:23:59.180 --> 00:24:04.500
might never find it again, the possibility
that their civilization is out there thriving

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:09.760
somewhere in the stars is a comfort after
so much devastation.

00:24:09.760 --> 00:24:15.140
Yet eventually, everything — no matter how
extraordinary – must come to an end.

00:24:15.140 --> 00:24:20.290
One might assume that Fellstar would last
beyond Eve, or perhaps beyond everything.

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:25.090
But while Fellstar doesn’t age or require
rest, they are not immortal.

00:24:25.090 --> 00:24:28.840
Like most machines, Fellstar isn’t built
to function forever.

00:24:28.840 --> 00:24:35.660
And so, they simply fall apart: piece by piece,
bit by bit, over the years, like a skeleton

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:36.810
on the plains.

00:24:36.810 --> 00:24:42.700
While Fellstar doesn’t mind, Eve does, using
scavenged parts to keep their dear friend

00:24:42.700 --> 00:24:46.390
functioning long past their natural ‘lifespan.’

00:24:46.390 --> 00:24:51.051
While both of them know Fellstar’s end is
near, they make every day the best they can

00:24:51.051 --> 00:24:55.370
— exploring new regions and cataloging new
species.

00:24:55.370 --> 00:25:01.440
When no easy fixes remain, and Fellstar can
no longer travel, Eve brings specimens directly

00:25:01.440 --> 00:25:03.630
to Fellstar instead.

00:25:03.630 --> 00:25:07.190
Small comforts to take their mind off the
enviable.

00:25:07.190 --> 00:25:12.230
Eve is prepared to take care of Fellstar forever,
but she knows they don’t want this.

00:25:12.230 --> 00:25:16.760
Fellstar doesn’t fear the end of their journey
like organic creatures do.

00:25:16.760 --> 00:25:22.940
In the end, Fellstar gestures for Eve to sit
beside them, and they spend one final moment

00:25:22.940 --> 00:25:24.600
together.

00:25:24.600 --> 00:25:30.090
When the spark that is Fellstar finally goes
out, all that is left is a cold shell.

00:25:30.090 --> 00:25:32.300
Eve knows that her friend is gone.

00:25:32.300 --> 00:25:37.940
She knows Fellstar’s body will stay where
it lies, untouched by animals and plants,

00:25:37.940 --> 00:25:41.820
slowly falling apart into fragments, but never
truly vanishing.

00:25:41.820 --> 00:25:44.750
It’s not a sight she can bare to see.

00:25:44.750 --> 00:25:48.990
So, not knowing what else to do, she moves
on.

00:25:48.990 --> 00:25:54.370
Reapers typically embrace solitude, but Eve
soon finds that being alone is not the same

00:25:54.370 --> 00:25:56.120
as being lonely.

00:25:56.120 --> 00:26:00.730
In time, she realizes that Fellstar would
want her to keep exploring.

00:26:00.730 --> 00:26:04.309
To see what else is still out there, beyond
the world they walked together.

00:26:04.309 --> 00:26:09.390
So, she decides to keep the adventure alive
in memory of her friend, and continue the

00:26:09.390 --> 00:26:11.830
pursuit of discovery…

00:26:11.830 --> 00:26:16.580
Setting out on her own, Eve has been forever
changed through her time with Fellstar, and

00:26:16.580 --> 00:26:20.809
seeks to be a benevolent force in an uncaring
world.

00:26:20.809 --> 00:26:26.360
She adopts an orphaned Foxtrotter, whom she
rears to adulthood as if it were her own child.

00:26:26.360 --> 00:26:31.860
And in time, she discovers other intelligent
Reapers like her, and becomes part of their

00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:32.860
flock.

00:26:32.860 --> 00:26:39.180
And so Fellstar, in life and death, is a catalyst
for change within Eve, expanding her worldview,

00:26:39.180 --> 00:26:44.920
and continuing an ancient chain of ideas shared
from one species to another, even after the

00:26:44.920 --> 00:26:47.440
Sea Stewards have long left Serina.

00:26:47.440 --> 00:26:52.900
Eve’s flock might very well be the last
group of Reapers under the sun, but they face

00:26:52.900 --> 00:26:54.179
their fate head on.

00:26:54.179 --> 00:26:59.490
For in the words of the author, everything
has its beginning, and so too everything has

00:26:59.490 --> 00:27:00.710
its end.

00:27:00.710 --> 00:27:03.320
But until that time, they will not stop living.

00:27:03.320 --> 00:27:05.060
They won't give up.

00:27:05.060 --> 00:27:10.480
One never knows how long their story might
be, but the world is wide, and life is full

00:27:10.480 --> 00:27:12.580
of surprises…

00:27:12.580 --> 00:27:15.200
The story of Serina isn’t over yet.

00:27:15.200 --> 00:27:20.400
The End Ultimocene — an era home to some
of the most unique lifeforms of all — is

00:27:20.400 --> 00:27:21.400
just beginning.

00:27:21.400 --> 00:27:23.910
But that’s all I can give away for now.

00:27:23.910 --> 00:27:28.590
If you find this project as incredible as
I do, I’d encourage you to check out the

00:27:28.590 --> 00:27:33.640
main website linked in the description and
read more of Dylan Bajda’s incredible project

00:27:33.640 --> 00:27:35.549
of Serina.

00:27:35.549 --> 00:27:38.050
And as always, thanks for watching.

00:27:38.050 --> 00:27:42.679
If you enjoyed this entry, please lend your
support by liking, subscribing, and hitting

00:27:42.679 --> 00:27:46.710
the notification icon to stay up to date on
all things Curious.

00:27:46.710 --> 00:27:59.740
See you in the next video.

